=== M4: the gate rule's own arithmetic (no data needed for the derivation) ===
observed P(unit h=6 | random) = 31/576 = 0.0538
  95% CI  [0.0354, 0.0722]
P(max over 576 random units < 6) = (1-p)^576 = 1.449e-14
  -> G-STOP was certain to within 1e-14
smallest p for which a 576-unit max-gate passes with prob >= 0.5: p <= 0.00120
  i.e. the null must produce a perfect unit less than once in 831 draws
and even on G-PASS the brief requires min(h_trained) > H*, so with H*=5
  ALL 18 trained units must score 6; with H*=6 the design is unfalsifiable-positive.

